# No autoFocus inside modals

Never add `autoFocus` to any input, textarea, or select that lives inside a modal, sheet, drawer, or overlay component (e.g. `ReceiptModal`, `DetailSheet`, `AddItemSheet`, `PasswordModal`).

On mobile, `autoFocus` immediately triggers the soft keyboard, which pushes the modal up or partially offscreen before the user can read the content.

```tsx
/* ✅ correct */
<input value={name} onChange={...} placeholder="Alex" />

/* ❌ never do this inside a modal */
<input autoFocus value={name} onChange={...} placeholder="Alex" />
```

The only exception is admin-side inline editors that are explicitly triggered by a user tap/click (e.g. the price edit field in `ItemCard` admin mode), where immediate focus is intentional and there is no modal container.
